{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":149491,"duration_api_ms":148164,"num_turns":18,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4d758dd4-3d07-456e-8ec4-04c0db338f39","total_cost_usd":0.81843025,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63159,"cache_read_input_tokens":533063,"output_tokens":6284,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63159,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":11,"outputTokens":6284,"cacheReadInputTokens":533063,"cacheCreationInputTokens":63159,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.81843025,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Thorough review of the save-schema versioning and migration scaffolding (tanksim-6e5.1.2.3). The implementation is well-structured and correct. Key strengths: (1) The migration registry pattern with compile-time assert (`MIGRATIONS.len() == SCHEMA_VERSION - MIN_SUPPORTED_SCHEMA`) guarantees migration chain integrity at compile time. (2) Two real migrations demonstrate the pattern — v2→v3 does a non-trivial rescaling of dissolved chemistry totals from gross to net water volume with comprehensive input validation, and v3→v4 is a no-op showing how serde defaults can be leveraged. (3) Three distinct error variants (SchemaVersionTooNew, SchemaVersionTooOld, SchemaMigration) provide clear, actionable error messages. (4) The migration contract is well-documented in doc comments with a 5-step checklist for adding new migrations. (5) 18 tests cover roundtrip save/load, deterministic resume, full migration chain (v2→current), malformed input rejection (missing fields, negative values, exceeded geometry bounds), future/old version rejection, carbonate cache repair, and stability tracker reseeding. (6) The API layer in tank_api properly integrates via `SaveFile::from_value()` and maps errors to appropriate HTTP status codes (400 for version issues, 500 for invariant violations). (7) Post-migration, the load path correctly normalizes carbonate state and reconciles the stability tracker before `into_engine()` runs invariant enforcement. All acceptance criteria are met: tests demonstrate migration application, unknown versions produce clear errors, and the migration path is documented for later contributors.","amendments":[]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"76618efd-fdd9-4979-b015-123fd41d7bfc"}
